27462 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The first stage\054 clustering\054 is the technique of grouping multiple wallet addresses on the blockchain into a single entity\056 Because a single user can generate hundreds or even thousands of wallet addresses\054 examining data at the level of individual addresses alone makes it difficult to identify the actual actor behind them\056 Clustering employs several techniques to solve this problem\056 The Common\055Input Heuristic\054 for example\054 infers that when multiple addresses are used as inputs in a single transaction\054 those addresses are controlled by the same user\056 The Change Address Heuristic analyzes the pattern of change addresses \024 the addresses to which remaining funds are returned after a payment \024 in UTXO3\051\055based blockchains\054 and groups them into the same entity\0563\051 Graph\055based connection analysis is layered on top of this\054 tracking a single user group within a network in which addresses and transactions are represented as nodes and edges\054 combining time\054 amounts\054 and behavioral      \176)
     /K [ 5 ]
     /P 27463 0 R
     /Pg 2462 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
