27502 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The greatest risk to guard against in labeling is false label propagation\056 If a single incorrect label spreads like a domino to other connected clusters\054 it can lead to the serious error of classifying a legitimate user\047s wallet as a suspicious address\056 The fact that labeling criteria and risk assessment logic are protected as trade secrets\054 making external verification impossible\054 amplifies this risk further \024 and it remains an important challenge for the industry\056\n\nThe third stage\054 pattern analysis\054 evaluates the level of risk and the likelihood of criminal activity by analyzing the behavioral patterns of labeled entities\056 The core task goes beyond identifying an entity to reading how that entity behaves\056 A cluster with frequent outflows and dispersed inflows is likely an exchange\073 small repeated transfers are classified as resembling phishing or scam patterns\073 sending large amounts to mixing services is interpreted as an attempted money laundering\056 Pattern analysis reveals abnormal behavior and hidden criminal signals through three methods\072 transaction flow analysis\054 behavioral analysis\054 and network analysis\056 This stage plays the most decisive role in anti\055money laundering \050AML\051 activity and criminal investigations\056)
     /K [ 3 ]
     /P 27503 0 R
     /Pg 3281 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
