27590 0 obj
  << /ActualText (In March 2022\054 the Lazarus Group \024 believed to be affiliated with North Korea \024 attacked the Ronin Bridge\054 the underlying network of the blockchain game Axie Infinity\056 The method of attack was sophisticated\056 Lazarus seized the private keys of five of the nine validators on the Ronin network\054 thereby obtaining transaction approval authority\054 and then used that authority to approve two fraudulent transactions\054 stealing approximately 173\054600 ETH and 25\0565 million USDC\05611\051\n\nImmediately after the theft\054 Lazarus launched a rapid dispersal operation to make the funds difficult to trace\056 The stolen funds were dispersed across multiple intermediary wallets\056 Chainalysis succeeded in visualizing this complex flow of funds through its Reactor tool\056 By organizing on\055chain data into graph structures\054 it traced step by step the routes through which the funds had moved\054 and reconstructed how billions of dollars\047 worth of stolen assets had been dispersed and mixed into a single flowchart\05612\051 This went beyond simple address tracking \024 it rendered the entirety of Lazarus\047s money laundering strategy visible\056\n\nElliptic also independently traced and published the money laundering routes and movement patterns through its own public analysis\056 Elliptic separately analyzed the proportion of stolen funds that had completed laundering and the routes through which they had entered exchanges\054 sharing these findings with law enforcement and exchanges\054 thereby enabling them to identify and respond to the relevant funds\05613\051 The analyses produced by the two firms complemented one another\054 enhancing the accuracy of the investigation\056)
     /K [ 4 ]
     /P 27591 0 R
     /Pg 5166 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

