  << /ActualText (In November 2024\054 the U\056S\056 Court of Appeals for the Fifth Circuit ruled that OFAC\031s sanctions against Tornado Cash\031s immutable smart contracts were unlawful\056 The court held that immutable smart contracts\054 which cannot be owned or controlled by any person\054 do not constitute \034property\035 subject to OFAC sanctions authority\056 In March 2025\054 the U\056S\056 Treasury removed Tornado Cash from the sanctions list\056 Criminal proceedings against individual developers\054 however\054 continue separately\056 This case illustrates that legal disputes concerning the scope of state sanctions authority over decentralized protocols remain unresolved\056 See Digital Asset\054 \034Why the U\056S\056 Court Ruled That Tornado Cash Could Not Be Sanctioned\054\035 November 27\054 2024\054 accessed May 8\054 2026\054 )
