27693 0 obj
  << /ActualText (In February 2025\054 the TraderTraitor organization \024 operating under North Korea\047s Reconnaissance General Bureau \024 carried out a hack of approximately \0441\0565 billion against major global crypto exchange Bybit\056 It was the largest single theft of its kind in history\056 The hackers compromised the software of a third\055party vendor that Bybit used for transaction signing\054 injecting malicious JavaScript that made it appear as though the exchange was signing ordinary transactions\054 and in doing so stole approximately 401\054000 ETH\056 The attack was disguised as a routine transfer of funds from a cold wallet to a hot wallet \024 a regular operational procedure within the exchange \024 making it exceptionally difficult to detect\056\n\nThe stolen funds were subsequently dispersed through various intermediary wallets and multiple networks\056 The hackers exchanged ETH for BTC and DAI \050a decentralized stablecoin collateralized by crypto assets\051 and alternated between decentralized exchanges \050DEXs\051\054 cross\055chain bridges\054 and KYC\055free instant swap services21\051 to complicate tracing efforts\056 Notably\054 a characteristic strategy of North Korean hacker groups was also observed\072 certain assets were left dormant for extended periods to avoid the heightened scrutiny of the                 \176)
     /K [ 5 ]
     /P 27694 0 R
     /Pg 7210 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

