27751 0 obj
  << /ActualText (In October 2025\054 the U\056S\056 Department of Justice and OFAC indicted Chen Zhi \024 chairman of Cambodia\055based Prince Group \024 on charges of wire fraud and money laundering\054 and seized 127\054271 BTC connected to him\056 It was the largest single\055case crypto seizure in the history of the U\056S\056 Department of Justice\056 Prince Group presented itself outwardly as a real estate\054 financial\054 and entertainment conglomerate\054 but was in reality a transnational criminal organization operating throughout Southeast Asia that combined human trafficking\054 forced labor\054 and online investment fraud\056 The organization lured victims through fraudulent job advertisements\054 confiscated their passports\054 and forced them to send scam messages\054 siphoning astronomical sums from victims around the world\05625\051\n\nWhere the first thread of the investigation came from cannot be confirmed from publicly available records alone\056 Yet examining the structure of the investigation allows for one reasonable inference\056 The reason investigators were able to detect fund movements in near real time and take immediate freezing action was that they had already identified in advance the wallet addresses Chen Zhi was using\056 The fact that China had been investigating Prince Group since at least 2020\054 that U\056S\056 investigators had been accumulating evidence over the course of several years\054 and that testimony from escaped victims and international cooperative investigations had been ongoing for years \024 all of this strongly suggests that off\055chain intelligence preceded and enabled the on\055chain tracing\05626\051 The most reasonable inference as to what made real\055time tracking possible in this case is the following structure\072 investigators shared with blockchain analytics firms the complex body of information obtained off\055chain \024 wallet addresses\054 exchange accounts\054 money laundering routes\054 associated individuals \024 and the analytics firms used that as the basis to reverse\055trace all connected fund flows and stitch the dispersed threads into a single coherent picture\056\n\nA further question remains\054 however\056 How was it possible to seize 127\054271 BTC held in a private wallet \024 that is\054 a wallet whose private key is held directly by the individual\054 not by an exchange or third party\077 Without the private key\054 access to the wallet is impossible by definition\056 The U\056S\056 Department of Justice has not disclosed how the private key was obtained\056 However\054 according to TRM Labs\047 analysis of the indictment\054 the charging documents state that Chen Zhi personally held the seed phrases for multiple wallets and that investigators recovered them in the course of the investigation\05627\051 The conclusion that can reasonably be drawn from publicly available materials is that years of accumulated off\055chain intelligence \024 informants\054 victim testimony\054 and leads obtained through search and seizure \024 made it possible to secure the private keys\056\n\nWhatever the precise method of obtaining the private keys\054 what is clear is that this seizure would not have been possible without the combination of off\055chain intelligence and on\055chain tracing\056 Once that combination had yielded a complete picture of the fund flows\054 investigators waited for the decisive moment\056 The United States and the United Kingdom jointly imposed sanctions on 146 targets connected to Prince Group and froze assets belonging to Chen Zhi\054      \176)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 27752 0 R
     /Pg 8611 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

