27814 0 obj
  << /ActualText (areas\056 The cases of these two firms demonstrate that blockchain analytics is not the exclusive capability of any single company\054 but a structural trend of sophistication advancing across the industry as a whole\056\n\nIn August 2024\054 TRM Labs joined forces with the TRON blockchain and Tether to form the T3 Financial Crime Unit\054 beginning direct intervention in the freezing of illicit funds\056 Within just four months of its launch\054 T3 achieved the freezing of over \044100 million in illicit USDT\054 with cumulative freezes subsequently surpassing \044300 million\05631\051 This structure \024 in which a private blockchain analytics firm\054 a blockchain network\054 and a stablecoin issuer formed a tripartite cooperative framework to directly counter illicit funds \024 is regarded as a case that advances the existing state\055private symbiosis model by one further step\056\n\nTRM Labs has also produced notable results in terrorist financing investigations\056 In terrorist financing cases resolved in Indonesia in 2024 and 2025\054 TRM Labs\047 on\055chain analysis was adopted as key evidence\056 Indonesia\047s Financial Intelligence Unit \050PPATK\051 and its counter\055terrorism police unit Detachment 88 used TRM Labs\047 analytical tools to trace and secure a conviction in court against a specific suspect who had transferred a total of \04449\054000 worth of USDT to an ISIS\055affiliated fundraising campaign in Syria across 15 transactions through an exchange\05632\051 This case \024 in which an Indonesian court recognized on\055chain blockchain data as core evidence in a terrorist financing prosecution \024 marked an important turning point in the establishment of crypto forensics as legally admissible evidence in Southeast Asia\056\n\nElliptic has distinguished itself in research on cross\055chain crime\056 According to Elliptic\047s 2025 research\054 the scale of cross\055chain crime reached \04421\0568 billion \024 more than triple the figures of \0444 billion in 2022 and \0447 billion in 2023 within just two to three years\054 illustrating how rapidly money laundering through cross\055chain asset movement is becoming more sophisticated\05633\051 In response\054 Elliptic has built an analytical framework covering more than 50 blockchains and more than 250 bridges\054 and major global exchanges including Coinbase and Revolut have adopted this solution as a core compliance tool\05634\051\n\nChainalysis visualizing Lazarus\047s money laundering routes\054 TRM Labs providing on\055chain analysis for terrorist financing investigations\054 Elliptic tracing the full picture of cross\055chain crime \024 the cases of these three firms demonstrate that blockchain analytics has matured from the capability of a single company into a structural capability of the industry as a whole\056 The scope of tracing is widening\054 the precision of analysis is deepening\054 and the speed of response is accelerating\056 And as this capability matures\054 so too does the confidence of states that crypto can be institutionalized\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 27815 0 R
     /Pg 10134 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

