27870 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The cases covered in Chapter 2 differ in character from one another\056 Nation\055state hacking\054 collapse driven by internal corruption\054 the largest theft in history\054 the dismantling of a transnational criminal organization\054 terrorist financing investigations\054 cross\055chain crime research \024 the types of crime\054 their scale\054 and their backgrounds are all different\056 Yet running across all of these cases\054 one thing has been repeatedly confirmed\072 for blockchain analytics to actually function\054 and for it to serve as the basis for institutionalization\054 three conditions must be met\056\n\nThe first condition is traceability\056 The anonymity of blockchain is growing thinner in the face of analytics technology\056 Whether funds dispersed across thousands of wallets\054 internal embezzlement of billions of dollars\054 the largest theft in history\054 criminal proceeds running into the tens of billions of dollars\054 or terrorist financing crossing borders \024 as long as it is recorded on\055chain\054 a thread for tracing necessarily exists\056 Through the process by which clustering groups scattered wallets into a single entity\054 labeling attaches a name to that entity\054 and pattern analysis evaluates the risk level of its behavior\054 anonymous addresses are gradually converted into identifiable actors\056 There is no such thing as complete anonymity\056 There is only data that has not yet been read\056\n\nThe second condition is the capacity for intervention\056 As tracing became possible\054 the state gained the ability to intervene\056 Behind all of these outcomes \024 the OFAC sanctions on Tornado Cash\054 the designation of Huione Pay as subject to special measures\054 the conviction of Sam Bankman\055Fried\054 the indictment of Chen Zhi and the largest crypto seizure in history \024 lay blockchain analytics data\056 The subjects of intervention have also expanded\056 As a public\055private cooperative ecosystem has formed that encompasses not only state agencies but also blockchain networks\054 stablecoin issuers\054 and exchanges\054 the response to illicit funds has become faster and more wide\055ranging\056\n\nThe third condition is real\055world connectivity\056 As on\055chain data has been admitted as evidence in courts\054 and as countries with different laws and institutions have come to share the same analytics platforms\054 the speed and scope of international cooperation have been transformed\056 The reality that an Indonesian court recognized blockchain data as core evidence in a terrorist    \176)
     /K [ 6 ]
     /P 27871 0 R
     /Pg 10550 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

