27906 0 obj
  << /ActualText (earliest cases in which blockchain data was used as decisive evidence in court\05637\051 In the course of the investigation\054 Haun made another discovery\072 within the crypto industry \024 widely regarded as a hotbed of illegality \024 companies like Coinbase were knocking on regulators\047 doors of their own accord\056 An industry that had been outside the institutional framework was trying to come in\05638\051\n\nHaun subsequently founded the first crypto investigation task force in U\056S\056 Department of Justice history and led inter\055agency cooperation on crypto investigations\056 After leaving the prosecutor\047s office\054 she joined the Coinbase board of directors\054 became a partner at Andreessen Horowitz running a crypto fund\054 and later struck out independently to establish Haun Ventures\054 a \0441\0565 billion fund\05639\051 This trajectory represents more than a simple career transition\056 In the field of investigation\054 Haun learned firsthand that while Bitcoin as a technology cannot itself be prosecuted\054 the traces it leaves can be traced \024 and that within the industry there exist companies willing to embrace regulation\056 Bitcoin cannot be eliminated\054 but it can be managed\056 And if it can be managed\054 the state will take it in\056 The person who grasped that logic before anyone else stepped down from the prosecutor\047s office and walked straight into the heart of that new industry\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 27907 0 R
     /Pg 12028 0 R
