27910 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The Travel Rule\054 MiCA\054 the spot Bitcoin ETF\054 and the GENIUS Act each have different purposes and backgrounds\054 but they share a common premise\072 none of them can function effectively in practice without blockchain analytics infrastructure\056\n\nThe Travel Rule is a regulation that the Financial Action Task Force \050FATF\051 applied to virtual asset service providers \050VASPs\051 in 2019\054 requiring that sender and recipient information be transmitted alongside crypto transfers between service providers such as exchanges \024 a transplantation of principles already applied in the traditional financial system into the crypto domain\05640\051 For this regulation to be implemented in substance\054 real\055time identification of counterparties and detection of suspicious transactions must be possible\056 The labeling  frameworks and KYT \050Know Your Transaction\051 solutions41\051 built by blockchain analytics firms function as the core infrastructure underpinning that implementation\056\n\nThe European Union\047s MiCA \050Markets in Crypto\055Assets\051 regulation\054 which entered into force in   \176)
     /K [ 2 ]
