  << /ActualText (was signed into law by President Trump\056 The GENIUS Act requires stablecoin issuers to maintain one\055to\055one reserves\054 comply with monthly disclosure obligations\054 and build AML and sanctions compliance programs\056 Notably\054 all issuers must possess the technical capability to freeze\054 seize\054 and burn stablecoins pursuant to legal orders\05645\051 The real\055time monitoring and sanctions compliance infrastructure that blockchain analytics firms have already built underpins the practical enforceability of this law\056\n\nThe arc from the founding of blockchain analytics firms\054 through the introduction of the Travel Rule\054 the implementation of MiCA\054 the approval of the spot Bitcoin ETF\054 and the enactment of the GENIUS Act is a process of co\055evolution in which technology and institutions have matured together\054 each reinforcing the other\056 These frameworks each have different purposes and backgrounds\054 but share the common premise that none can function effectively without blockchain analytics infrastructure\056 Within a structure in which technology opens the door to regulatory enforceability and regulation in turn expands demand for technology\054 analytics infrastructure and institutionalization have made each other increasingly indispensable\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 27975 0 R
     /Pg 13026 0 R
