28008 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Decentralization remains one of the most frequently invoked terms in the crypto community\056 Decentralized Finance \050DeFi\051\054 Decentralized Autonomous Organizations \050DAOs\051\054 Decentralized Exchanges \050DEXs\051 \024 the rhetoric of decentralization has in fact proliferated into an ever wider range of forms\056 Yet when one looks at the actual structure\054 a different picture emerges\056\n\nThe overwhelming majority of crypto transactions still take place through centralized exchanges \050CEXs\051\056 Binance\054 Coinbase\054 Upbit and their peers require KYC\054 operate under government regulation\054 and have adopted blockchain analytics solutions to monitor transactions\056 The Bitcoin network itself is decentralized\054 but the gateway through which most people access Bitcoin is thoroughly centralized\056 It is a structure in which centralized infrastructure has been layered on top of decentralized technology\056\n\nThe stablecoin ecosystem tells the same story\056 USDT and USDC \024 which underpin the liquidity of DeFi \024 are issued by Tether and Circle respectively\054 both centralized private companies\056 These companies hold the authority to freeze assets at specific addresses in accordance with U\056S\056 financial regulations including OFAC sanctions\056 The core liquidity of what is called decentralized finance sits under the control of centralized issuers\056\n\nThe data concentration of blockchain analytics firms is another form of structural centralization\056 The labeling data built by a small number of private firms \024 Chainalysis\054 Elliptic\054 TRM Labs \024 has become the de facto standard shared by investigative agencies\054 financial institutions\054 and exchanges worldwide\056 The authority to determine which addresses are dangerous and which transactions are suspicious on\055chain has become concentrated in the hands of these few companies\056 Blockchain is distributed\054 but the power to interpret blockchain is concentrated\056 The rhetoric of decentralization remains\054 but the structure has already been moving in a different direction\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 28009 0 R
     /Pg 13670 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

