28025 0 obj
  << /ActualText (What\054 then\054 is institutionalized crypto\077 It is not the stateless money Satoshi dreamed of\056 Nor is it identical to the existing financial system\056 Institutionalized crypto sits somewhere in between\056\n\nCrypto now serves two functions simultaneously\056 The first is as infrastructure that extends dollar hegemony into the digital realm\056 As dollar stablecoins become the medium of global crypto transactions\054 and as the GENIUS Act obliges stablecoin issuers to hold U\056S\056 Treasuries\054 the crypto ecosystem has become a structural instrument for extending the dollar\047s digital domain\056 From the American perspective\054 crypto is not a threat to dollar hegemony but a new layer that reinforces it\056\n\nThe second is as infrastructure for financial innovation\056 Blockchain technology continues to work through problems that traditional finance has failed to solve \024 payments\054 clearing\054 asset tokenization\054 decentralized finance\056 Institutionalization has not entirely extinguished crypto\047s potential for innovation\056 In some respects\054 institutionalization has actually accelerated the pace of innovation by bringing in institutional capital and regulatory clarity\056\n\nWhat matters\054 however\054 is that neither of these two registers places at its core what Satoshi originally intended\072 the economic autonomy of individuals\054 free from states and financial institutions\056 That vision remains as the founding narrative of crypto\047s origin story\054 but it is no longer the animating principle that governs how crypto actually operates\056 Crypto was born as an instrument of freedom\054 but has grown into institutionalized financial infrastructure\056 And it was blockchain analytics technology that created the conditions for that growth\056 The question now is who\054 within the institutionalized crypto order\054 will analyze\054 interpret\054 and design the rules\056 It is precisely at this point that South Korea\047s position and challenges come into view\056)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 28026 0 R
     /Pg 14069 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

