28171 0 obj
  << /ActualText (following its founding in 2014\054 secured its first customers by supporting dark web investigations\054 and grew in earnest by directly demonstrating to U\056S\056 law enforcement agencies that its tracing tools could identify the perpetrators of the Mt\056 Gox hack\05660\051 TRM Labs\054 from its earliest days\054 recruited former government investigators as core personnel and \024 despite being a latecomer \024 rapidly built credibility in the law enforcement market\05661\051 Given that cooperation with investigative agencies was the core growth driver for both firms\054 this structure is a replicable model for South Korea\056 South Korea\047s National Police Agency\054 prosecution services\054 and financial authorities need to institutionally design a virtuous cycle in which they actively support startups in the blockchain analytics space\054 bring early\055stage startups in as partners on joint investigation projects\054 and ensure that the outputs of those projects accumulate as a labeling database\056 When investigative agencies function as both early customers and collaborators\054 private analytical capability can grow on the foundation of public trust and data\056\n\nA phased approach is needed to implement these three directions\056 In the short term\054 a joint on\055chain analytics task force involving the FIU\054 the Prosecution Service\054 the National Police Agency\054 and major exchanges should be established to integrate on\055chain data currently fragmented across institutions\054 and substantive legislative discussion should begin on strategic regulatory measures including spot virtual asset ETF introduction\054 derivatives regulation reform\054 and tax clarification\056 In the medium term\054 a Korean on\055chain analytics database equipped with clustering and labeling frameworks should be built as formal infrastructure\054 on the basis of data accumulated through pilot projects\056 In the long term\054 investigative agencies and financial authorities should conclude government contracts with domestic blockchain analytics startups on a project\055by\055project basis and prioritize their use in the compliance market\054 institutionally underpinning the growth of a private analytics ecosystem\056\n\nThere is a reason the development of independent analytical capability is especially urgent for South Korea\056 The Lazarus Group has repeatedly targeted South Korean virtual asset infrastructure\054 including Upbit\054 the country\047s largest exchange\05662\051 Building South Korea\047s own on\055chain analytical capability is not simply a matter of competition in financial infrastructure \024 it is a task directly linked to national security\056 Internalizing Korean on\055chain analytical capability\054 designing the regulatory framework in the vocabulary of strategy rather than defense\054 and cultivating specialist talent and a corporate ecosystem in the analytics technology space \024 this is how South Korea can survive in an era of crypto institutionalization governed by traceable money\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 28172 0 R
     /Pg 17633 0 R
