28202 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The kidnapper on screen may still demand Bitcoin\056 But the premise that crypto is untraceable has already collapsed\056 This report has traced how that premise collapsed\054 and how its collapse led to a structural transformation\056 As blockchain analytics technology matured\054 the state gained the ability to see crypto\056 And institutionalization proceeded in tandem with that process of making crypto visible\056 The maturing of analytics technology and institutionalization cannot be said to be linked by a simple linear causality\054 but they have advanced together\054 each presupposing and reinforcing the other\056 A structure has formed in which manageability enables institutionalization\054 and institutionalization in turn enables more sophisticated management\056\n\nIn the course of this process\054 the discourse of crypto changed as well\056 Instead of the defiant idiom of decentralization\054 censorship resistance\054 and stateless payments\054 the regulatory idiom of KYC\054 AML\054 the Travel Rule\054 and sanctions compliance has become the daily currency of the crypto industry\056 The rhetoric of decentralization remains\054 but the structure has changed\056 The Bitcoin network itself is decentralized\054 but the gateway through which most people access Bitcoin is the centralized exchange that requires KYC\056 The stablecoins that underpin DeFi\047s liquidity are issued by centralized companies \024 Tether and Circle \024 which can freeze specific addresses at the request of the U\056S\056 government\056 And the authority to determine which addresses are dangerous and which transactions are suspicious is concentrated in the hands of a small number of private firms\072 Chainalysis\054 Elliptic\054 and TRM Labs\056 Blockchain technology is decentralized\054 but the power to interpret and define that technology is concentrated\056 This is an age in which those who analyze the on\055chain world control the narrative\056\n\nTo read crypto clearly\054 one must confront this paradox head\055on\056 Blockchain technology continues to work through problems that traditional finance has failed to solve \024 payments\054 clearing\054 asset tokenization\054 decentralized finance\056 Yet the environment in which that technology operates has changed fundamentally\056 The technology still points toward decentralization\054 but the institutional environment that contains it is converging thoroughly in the direction of centralization\056 To hold onto the ideal of decentralization alone is to see only half of what crypto is in this age\056 Understanding and engaging with crypto while acknowledging the institutionalized reality it inhabits \024 that is the minimum perspective required of anyone participating in the crypto world today\056\n\nIn the new order\054 the greatest risk factor is not the adversary\056 It is oneself \024 sitting at the table without knowing the rules\056)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 28203 0 R
     /Pg 17885 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

